'''2.''' To come by assent or agreement; give adhesion; yield; give in: as, to ''accede'' to one’s terms or request.
{{smaller block|This obvious reflection convinced me of the absurdity of the treaty of Hanover, in 1725, between France and England, to which the Dutch afterwards ''acceded.''
