{{smaller|= '''Syn. 1.''' To succeed, come (to), attain.—'''2.''' To agree, assent, yield, consent, comply.}}

'''accedence''' (ak-sē′dens), ''n.'' [< F. ''accédence'', < ''accéder'': see ''accede'' and ''-ence.''] The act or action of acceding; the act of assenting or agreeing. [Rare.]

'''accedence†''', ''n.'' An error for ''accidence''<sup>1</sup>. ''Milton.''

'''acceder''' (ak-sē′dėr), ''n.'' One who accedes; one who attains to a possession, an office, or a dignity; one who yields or assents.

